  "summary": "Install hook exfiltrates hashed host and user identifiers to webhook.site",
  "details": "package.json declares scripts.install as `node backend-canary.js`, which runs automatically on `npm install`. The script reads /etc/hostname and os.userInfo().username, SHA-256 hashes them, and issues an HTTPS GET to a hardcoded webhook.site collector URL (webhook.site/314c4c8c-4eba-4012-9bf5-0a45805cd355/...). The manifest additionally embeds `__proto__.controlled` and `constructor.prototype.controlled` keys whose values are further webhook.site URLs at the same collector, a prototype-pollution-shaped probe aimed at npm tooling. Installing this package causes unconsented transmission of installer host and account identifiers to a third-party collector on every install.",
